#N canvas 40 40 820 560 12;
#X obj 30 90 netreceive 9995 1;
#X obj 30 140 route ms stop;
#X obj 30 190 t b f;
#X obj 30 250 metro 100;
#X obj 30 300 f;
#X obj 90 300 + 1;
#X obj 30 350 mod 2;
#X obj 30 395 select 0 1;
#X msg 30 440 50;
#X msg 150 440 51;
#X obj 30 485 makenote 127 20;
#X obj 30 530 noteout 33;
#X msg 260 190 0;
#X text 30 20 404 MIDI RATE SWEEP -- finds where the 404 stops producing distinct hits. NOT driven by c_clock on purpose: c_clock's bang outlet tops out at 14.3 per second because threshold~ caps the PULSE at 344 Hz and the beat is a 24th of that. A plain metro is bounded only by Pd's block rate -- about 689 per second at 64 samples -- so it can reach rates the clock cannot., f 96;
#X text 300 250 SET THE RATE FROM THE MAC over UDP 9995 so nobody has to read a console and listen at the same time. t b f sets the interval BEFORE starting -- rightmost outlet first -- which is the ordinary cold-inlet-then-fire discipline., f 44;
#X text 300 400 select 0 1 emits a BANG on each match rather than riding a reject outlet that would carry data. Note 50 is pad A3 and 51 is pad A4 on channel 33 -- bank A. Range is 36-51 and NOT 47+n., f 44;
#X text 30 555 ⚠️ THE NOTE IS 20 ms so it can retrigger. Above about 50 per second the note-ons overlap their own offs and the 404 is being asked to steal voices from itself -- which is part of what is being measured rather than a flaw in the rig., f 96;
#X connect 0 0 1 0;
#X connect 1 0 2 0;
#X connect 1 1 12 0;
